From: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: re-arm only after the flow
 count has moved

A refresh from the flowtable means software is still forwarding the
cookie. ppe_offload_flow_stale() takes a hit counter that has not moved
since the previous refresh as the sign that the hardware entry stopped
matching, and answers -EEXIST so the refresh re-programs the flow. A
freshly programmed entry can be refreshed several times before the first
packet is counted, so two consecutive refreshes both read zero and the
identical entry is re-programmed for nothing.

Treat a frozen counter as stale only once the counter has been seen to
move. An entry that has never matched is not re-armed; the case the
check exists for, a counter that moved and then froze, is unchanged.

Measured on TP-Link Archer BE800 (IPQ9574): the re-arm lines at flow
setup drop from a few per new flow to none, IPv4 NAT stays at 2.35
Gbit/s with the CPU idle.

Signed-off-by: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-04 00:15:58
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-04 00:15:58
@@ -271,9 +271,13 @@
 	unsigned long lastused;
 	/* Packet count at the last refresh the flowtable sent for this
 	 * cookie, and whether one was seen at all (ppe_offload_flow_stale()).
+	 * refresh_moving records that the count was once seen to advance, so
+	 * a frozen count only counts as stale for an entry that has actually
+	 * matched before.
 	 */
 	u64 refresh_packets;
 	bool refresh_seen;
+	bool refresh_moving;
 	/* Re-points within the current PPE_OFFLOAD_FDB_FLAP_WINDOW, see
 	 * ppe_offload_fdb_move_work().
 	 */
@@ -912,7 +916,10 @@
  * frozen, conntrack still marked offloaded). Answering -EEXIST forever
  * keeps such a zombie; dropping it lets this very refresh program the flow
  * afresh. An entry superseded in the table (flow_valid clear) is stale by
- * definition. The first refresh only takes the baseline.
+ * definition. The first refresh only takes the baseline, and a frozen
+ * count is only stale once the count has been seen to move at least once,
+ * so the refreshes a fresh cookie gets before its first packet is counted
+ * do not re-arm it.
  */
 static bool ppe_offload_flow_stale(struct ppe_offload_priv *priv,
 				   struct ppe_offload_flow_entry *entry)
@@ -933,10 +940,21 @@
 
 	if (ppe_offload_counter_delta(packets, entry->refresh_packets,
 				      PPE_IN_FLOW_CNT_TBL_PKT_MAX)) {
+		entry->refresh_moving = true;
 		entry->refresh_packets = packets;
 		return false;
 	}
 
+	/* A frozen count only means the entry stopped matching if it was
+	 * ever matching. The flowtable can refresh a freshly programmed
+	 * cookie a few times before its first packet is counted, and a
+	 * direction that has simply not carried a packet yet would
+	 * otherwise be "re-armed" with the identical key, which changes
+	 * nothing. Require the count to have moved at least once first.
+	 */
+	if (!entry->refresh_moving)
+		return false;
+
 	return true;
 }
 
@@ -1973,6 +1991,7 @@
 	entry->dsa_index = dp->index;
 	entry->stats_packets = 0;
 	entry->refresh_seen = false;
+	entry->refresh_moving = false;
 	entry->stats_bytes = 0;
 
 	return 0;
